  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 176175,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Nayruuu/NgSharp",
  "published": "2026-07-28T07:28:00.613Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.0 — the V3 engine.\n\nFused single-pass parser, lazy zero-copy model reads, monomorphic inline\ncaches, span-formatted pipes: the fastest of six benchmarked .NET template\nengines, warm and cold, in time and allocations, with byte-identical output.\n\nNEW\n- @switch / @case / @default control-flow block (both dialects)\n- TemplateOptions: one options record on every call (mode, strict, culture, limits)\n- Strict mode + Validate() diagnostics; silent failures become NgSharpException — including statically-detectable always-false conditions and literal division by zero\n- TemplateMode.Text: plain-text / JSON / CSV output through the same pipeline\n- TextWriter sinks + RenderAsync: awaited writes, atomic (a throwing render writes nothing)\n- $index / $count / $first / $last loop variables; per-render culture; RenderLimits caps\n- <ng-template> / @render fragments; transparent ng-container; @for (x of items)\n- [else-if] / [else] attribute chains; complex-type component property binding\n- 7 new built-in pipes (default, currency, lower, truncate, join, titlecase, pad) + [empty] directive\n\nBREAKING (each with its remedy in the README, section \"Migrating from 2.x\")\n- HtmlBuilder.Default removed: use Create() and keep the instance you register on\n- BuildFromTemplateAsync wrappers removed: rendering is synchronous\n- MinifyHtml and Token removed\n- FromObject / FromJson lose their unused parent/key parameters\n- FromJson reads the JsonElement lazily: Clone() an element that outlives its JsonDocument\n- NgElement.Key always returns string.Empty\n- The built-in pipes are sealed",
